# The `radios` producer: the radio userland facts, as three disjoint packages.
#
# Plain `KEY=value` lines only: no logic, no command substitution, no
# expansion. Safe to source from bash and to parse with grep/sed from anything
# else, and checked for that shape by os/rootfs/packages-src/build-deb.sh
# before it is sourced. os/rootfs/packages-src/README.md documents every field.

# Three packages, one producer. They are separate because a board chooses Wi-Fi
# client, access point and Bluetooth INDEPENDENTLY; one `mos-radio` would make
# a Bluetooth-only board install wpasupplicant and hostapd, and a combined
# Wi-Fi package would make a station-only board install hostapd. No path and no
# relationship is shared between them.
PACKAGES="mos-wifi mos-wifi-ap mos-bluetooth"

# `all` and not `amd64 arm64`. Every payload here is a shell script, a systemd
# unit or a symlink, with no ELF anywhere, so one archive is correct for every
# image this repository builds.
ARCHES="all"

# `family` is os/rootfs/packages-src itself, and it is here for one file: the
# shared copyright. The primary build context is this producer's OWN
# directory, so anything held in common with the sibling producers sits one
# level up and has to be named to be reachable.
#
# The unit bodies and the HCI-attach program are copied BYTE-IDENTICAL out of
# the tree the stage chain ships them from today, so that packaging them cannot
# become a second, drifting rendering of the same files. They live under
# os/boards/cx3576 because that is where the stage chain reads them from; their
# content is a radio-application fact, not a board fact -- the board facts they
# are paired with (/etc/mos/bt.conf, the radio kernel modules, the firmware)
# stay in mos-board-cx3576.
BUILD_CONTEXTS="family=os/rootfs/packages-src radio-units=os/boards/cx3576/overlay/etc/systemd/system radio-hwinit=os/boards/cx3576/hwinit"

# Only mos-bluetooth enables a unit at multi-user.target: mos-bt.service.
# mos-wifi and mos-wifi-ap each ship a local-fs.target.wants link instead,
# which this field does not count, so both write the zero rather than leaving a
# reader to infer it from a payload that does contain enablement links.
ENABLEMENT="mos-wifi=0 mos-wifi-ap=0 mos-bluetooth=1"
